The desk merged every date-wrong report into [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) and marked it known:
one parser, one fix. `causeOf` in `#lib/kb/causes` disagrees. Unique reports (export pages
overlap) group into **two** causes. Intake tags are a browser guess; the cause follows the
tenant locale and which booking form they run.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Two bugs were merged on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Each cause has its own GitHub ticket with the report count.
</Callout>

## Tickets

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 Oct. Our tickets follow that:

- parser → [Typhoonic/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/Typhoonic/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) — **fixed.** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- hint → [Typhoonic/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/Typhoonic/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) — **won't fix.** booking-v3 form retired.

Five reports the desk read as a one-day move still classify as `parser` by tenant. They stay a
footnote on that cause, not a third ticket.

